RCQ for iOS — Third-Party Attributions
=======================================

This product includes software developed by third parties. Each
upstream project's full license text lives at the path indicated.


libsignal
---------
Path: RCQ/Vendor/libsignal/
Project: https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later
License text: RCQ/Vendor/libsignal/LICENSE

Used for end-to-end encryption: X3DH key agreement, Double Ratchet
session ratcheting, sealed-sender envelope encryption, Kyber-based
PQXDH where peers are upgraded. Vendored unmodified at the version
pinned in `RCQ/Vendor/libsignal/Cargo.lock`. Linked into the iOS
binary; the AGPL-3.0 obligation propagates to the RCQ application
itself, which is consequently also distributed under AGPL-3.0
(see top-level LICENSE).


WebRTC (stasel/WebRTC)
----------------------
Project: https://github.com/stasel/WebRTC
License: BSD-3-Clause (Google's libwebrtc upstream license)
Distributed via: Swift Package Manager

Used for 1:1 voice / video calls and the audio-room mesh
(WebRTC.framework). Pre-built xcframework binary; we don't vendor
or modify the source.


